"""Cybersecurity glossary, part 22: recon and design principles, risk and resilience, defender and tester tools, secure channels and privacy.
Row = (id, English name, aliases, category, photo query, local names {fr,sw,rw} or None, en_meaning, en_use, fr_meaning, fr_use, rw_meaning, rw_use, sw_meaning, sw_use)
Awareness-level, protective content: it names tools and techniques so people and defenders can recognise and manage them; use tools only on systems you own or have written permission to test.
Kinyarwanda and Kiswahili are a DRAFT for review by fluent speakers."""
from cyber_terms_20 import R

TERMS_22 = [
    R("enumeration-banner-grabbing", "Enumeration, banner grabbing and ping sweeps", ["enumeration", "banner grabbing", "ping sweep", "host discovery", "service enumeration", "network enumeration", "fingerprinting services"], "attacks", "network map with hosts and open doors",
      {"fr": "Énumération, bannières et balayage ping", "sw": "Uorodheshaji wa mtandao na banner grabbing", "rw": "Gutahura ibikoresho n'serivisi ku muyoboro"},
      ("Early reconnaissance steps: a ping sweep checks which devices on a network answer, enumeration lists what they offer (services, shared folders, user names), and banner grabbing reads the greeting text a service sends, which often shows its software and version.", "Defenders see this as scanning noise in logs. Reduce it with firewalls that drop unneeded probes, hiding version banners, removing unused services, patching, and alerts on one source touching many hosts. Scan only networks you are authorised to test."),
      ("Étapes de reconnaissance : un balayage ping vérifie quels appareils répondent, l'énumération liste ce qu'ils offrent (services, dossiers partagés, noms d'utilisateurs) et la capture de bannière lit le texte d'accueil d'un service, qui révèle souvent logiciel et version.", "Les défenseurs y voient du bruit de scan dans les journaux. Réduisez-le : pare-feu qui ignore les sondes inutiles, bannières de version masquées, services inutiles retirés, correctifs et alertes quand une source touche beaucoup d'hôtes. Ne scannez que des réseaux autorisés."),
      ("Intambwe za mbere zo gutohoza: ping sweep irebera ibikoresho bisubiza ku muyoboro, enumeration irondora ibyo bitanga (serivisi, ububiko busangiwe, amazina y'abakoresha), naho banner grabbing isoma ubutumwa bwo kwakira serivisi butanga, akenshi bwerekana porogaramu n'ubwoko bwayo.", "Abarinzi bayibona nk'urusaku rwo gusuzuma muri logs. Rugabanye ukoresheje firewall ireka ibigeragezo bitari ngombwa, guhisha version, gukuraho serivisi zitakoreshwa, ivugurura n'imenyesha igihe aho kimwe kigerageza ibikoresho byinshi. Suzuma gusa imiyoboro wemerewe."),
      ("Hatua za awali za upelelezi: ping sweep hukagua vifaa vipi vinajibu kwenye mtandao, enumeration huorodhesha wanachotoa (huduma, folda zilizoshirikiwa, majina ya watumiaji), na banner grabbing husoma maandishi ya kukaribisha ya huduma, ambayo mara nyingi huonyesha programu na toleo.", "Watetezi huiona kama kelele ya skani kwenye kumbukumbu. Ipunguze kwa firewall inayodondosha majaribio yasiyo ya lazima, kuficha toleo, kuondoa huduma zisizotumika, masasisho na tahadhari chanzo kimoja kikigusa wapangishi wengi. Skani mitandao uliyoruhusiwa tu.")),
    R("secure-design-principles", "Secure design principles (fail-safe defaults, economy of mechanism, complete mediation, open design)", ["saltzer and schroeder", "saltzer schroeder principles", "fail-safe defaults", "fail safe defaults", "economy of mechanism", "complete mediation", "open design", "separation of privilege", "least common mechanism", "psychological acceptability", "secure design principles", "design principles of security"], "foundations", "blueprint with a lock and checklist",
      {"fr": "Principes de conception sécurisée", "sw": "Kanuni za usanifu salama", "rw": "Amahame yo gushushanya umutekano"},
      ("Classic rules for secure design (Saltzer and Schroeder, 1975): deny by default (fail-safe defaults), keep it simple (economy of mechanism), check every access every time (complete mediation), do not rely on a secret design (open design), need two conditions for sensitive actions (separation of privilege), least privilege, share little between users and make security easy to use (psychological acceptability).", "Use them as a checklist when designing apps, networks and policies: if a feature fails, does it fail closed? Is every request checked? Would people bypass it because it is too hard? They are principles, not a certificate of security."),
      ("Règles classiques pour concevoir des systèmes sûrs (Saltzer et Schroeder, 1975) : refus par défaut, conception simple, contrôle de chaque accès à chaque fois, pas de secret de conception, plusieurs conditions pour les actions sensibles, moindre privilège, partage minimal entre utilisateurs et sécurité facile à utiliser.", "Servez-vous-en comme liste de contrôle pour concevoir applications, réseaux et politiques : en cas de panne, le système se ferme-t-il ? Chaque requête est-elle vérifiée ? Les gens contourneront-ils une mesure trop pénible ? Ce sont des principes, pas un certificat de sécurité."),
      ("Amategeko ya kera yo kubaka sisitemu zirinzwe (Saltzer na Schroeder, 1975): kwanga byose ku mwanzuro, igishushanyo cyoroshye, kugenzura buri gihe ubwinjire bwose, kudashingira ku bishushanyo by'ibanga, gusaba ibintu birenze kimwe ku bikorwa by'ingenzi, uburenganzira bukeya bushoboka, gusangira bike hagati y'abakoresha no korohereza abantu gukoresha umutekano.", "Yakoreshwe nk'urutonde rwo kugenzura igihe utegura porogaramu, imiyoboro n'amabwiriza: iyo bigize ikibazo bifunga? Buri cyifuzo kiragenzurwa? Abantu bazabirenga kuko bigoye? Ni amahame, si icyemezo cy'umutekano."),
      ("Kanuni za kale za kujenga mifumo salama (Saltzer na Schroeder, 1975): kukataa kwa chaguo-msingi, muundo rahisi, kukagua kila ufikiaji kila mara, kutotegemea siri ya muundo, masharti zaidi ya moja kwa vitendo nyeti, haki ndogo kabisa, kushiriki kidogo kati ya watumiaji na usalama rahisi kutumia.", "Zitumie kama orodha ya kukagua unapobuni programu, mitandao na sera: ikishindwa, inafunga? Kila ombi linakaguliwa? Watu wataipita kwa sababu ni ngumu? Ni kanuni, si cheti cha usalama.")),
    R("risk-treatment", "Risk treatment (accept, avoid, transfer, mitigate; inherent and residual risk)", ["risk treatment", "risk response", "risk acceptance", "risk avoidance", "risk transfer", "risk mitigation", "residual risk", "inherent risk", "risk appetite", "risk tolerance", "treat accept transfer avoid", "risk management options"], "governance", "scale balancing risk options",
      {"fr": "Traitement du risque", "sw": "Matibabu ya hatari", "rw": "Gucunga ibyago (kwemera, kwirinda, kwimura, kugabanya)"},
      ("After assessing a risk you choose a response: avoid it (stop the activity), mitigate it (add controls), transfer or share it (for example insurance or a supplier contract) or accept it knowingly. Inherent risk is the level before controls, residual risk what remains after them. Risk appetite is how much risk an organisation is willing to pursue; tolerance is the acceptable variation around it.", "Record each decision in a risk register with an owner and a review date. Accepting a risk must be a conscious, approved decision, not a silent default, and insurance transfers some cost, not the responsibility to protect people's data."),
      ("Après évaluation d'un risque on choisit : l'éviter (arrêter l'activité), l'atténuer (ajouter des contrôles), le transférer (assurance, contrat) ou l'accepter en connaissance de cause. Le risque inhérent est celui d'avant les contrôles, le risque résiduel celui qui reste. L'appétence est le niveau de risque que l'organisation accepte ; la tolérance, l'écart acceptable.", "Consignez chaque décision dans un registre des risques avec un responsable et une date de revue. Accepter un risque doit être une décision consciente et approuvée ; l'assurance transfère un coût, pas l'obligation de protéger les données."),
      ("Nyuma yo gusuzuma ikibazo uhitamo igisubizo: kukirinda (guhagarika igikorwa), kukigabanya (wongeraho uburyo bwo kurinda), kukimurira abandi cyangwa kugisangira (urugero ubwishingizi cyangwa amasezerano) cyangwa kukemera ubizi. Ibyago bya mbere ni ibyo mbere yo kurinda, ibisigaye ni ibyago bisigaye. Appetite ni ibyago ikigo cyemera gukora; tolerance ni itandukaniro ryemewe.", "Andika buri cyemezo muri risk register ufite nyiracyo n'itariki yo kongera kureba. Kwemera ibyago bigomba kuba icyemezo cyemejwe, si ubusa; ubwishingizi bwimura igiciro, si inshingano yo kurinda amakuru."),
      ("Baada ya kutathmini hatari unachagua jibu: kuikwepa (kusimamisha shughuli), kuipunguza (kuongeza vidhibiti), kuihamisha au kuishiriki (mfano bima au mkataba wa muuzaji) au kuikubali kwa kujua. Hatari ya asili ni kabla ya vidhibiti, hatari iliyobaki ni inayobaki baada yake. Hamu ya hatari ni kiasi shirika linachotaka kuchukua; uvumilivu ni tofauti inayokubalika.", "Rekodi kila uamuzi kwenye rejista ya hatari ukiwa na mmiliki na tarehe ya mapitio. Kukubali hatari lazima iwe uamuzi ulioidhinishwa, si chaguo-msingi la kimya; bima huhamisha gharama, si wajibu wa kulinda data.")),
    R("bia-recovery-sites", "Business impact analysis (BIA) and recovery sites (hot, warm, cold)", ["business impact analysis", "bia", "hot site", "warm site", "cold site", "recovery site", "alternate site", "disaster recovery site", "maximum tolerable downtime", "mtd"], "operations", "backup office with servers ready",
      {"fr": "Analyse d'impact sur l'activité (BIA) et sites de secours", "sw": "Uchambuzi wa athari kwa biashara (BIA) na tovuti za dharura", "rw": "Isesengura ry'ingaruka ku bikorwa (BIA) n'ahantu ho gusubira"},
      ("A BIA finds the services an organisation cannot do without, what each hour of downtime costs, and so sets the targets RTO (how fast to restore) and RPO (how much data loss is acceptable). A recovery site is where work resumes: a hot site is ready and mirrored (fast, costly), a warm site has equipment but needs data restored, a cold site is only space and power (cheap, slow).", "Do a BIA before buying backup solutions, so spending matches what truly matters. Test the plan: a recovery site or a backup never exercised often fails on the day it is needed."),
      ("Une BIA identifie les services indispensables, ce que coûte chaque heure d'arrêt, et fixe ainsi le RTO (rapidité de reprise) et le RPO (perte de données acceptable). Un site de secours est l'endroit où l'on reprend : site chaud prêt et synchronisé (rapide, coûteux), tiède avec équipements mais données à restaurer, froid simple local avec électricité (peu cher, lent).", "Faites une BIA avant d'acheter des solutions de sauvegarde pour que les dépenses suivent l'essentiel. Testez le plan : un site ou une sauvegarde jamais exercés échouent souvent le jour J."),
      ("BIA igaragaza serivisi ikigo kidashobora kubaho tudafite, igiciro cya buri saha yo guhagarara, bityo igena RTO (vuba gute gusubiza) na RPO (amakuru yemewe gutakara). Ahantu ho gusubira: hot site yiteguye kandi ihuje amakuru (vuba, ihenze), warm site ifite ibikoresho ariko amakuru agomba kugarurwa, cold site ni umwanya n'amashanyarazi gusa (ihendutse, itinda).", "Kora BIA mbere yo kugura ibisubizo bya backup kugira ngo amafaranga akoreshwe ku by'ingenzi. Gerageza gahunda: aho gusubira cyangwa backup itigeze igeragezwa akenshi inanirwa umunsi ikenewe."),
      ("BIA hutambua huduma ambazo shirika haliwezi kuishi bila hizo, gharama ya kila saa ya kusimama, na hivyo huweka malengo RTO (haraka kiasi gani kurejesha) na RPO (upotevu wa data unaokubalika). Tovuti ya dharura: hot site iko tayari na imeakisiwa (haraka, ghali), warm site ina vifaa lakini data hurejeshwa, cold site ni nafasi na umeme tu (nafuu, polepole).", "Fanya BIA kabla ya kununua suluhisho za nakala rudufu ili matumizi yalingane na muhimu. Jaribu mpango: tovuti au nakala rudufu isiyowahi kujaribiwa mara nyingi hushindwa siku inapohitajika.")),
    R("high-availability-failover", "High availability, redundancy, failover and load balancing", ["high availability", "redundancy", "failover", "load balancer", "load balancing", "single point of failure", "spof", "fault tolerance", "ha cluster", "uptime"], "network", "two servers sharing the load",
      {"fr": "Haute disponibilité, redondance, basculement et répartition de charge", "sw": "Upatikanaji wa juu, uduplishaji na kubadilisha kiotomatiki", "rw": "Kuboneka igihe cyose, gukoresha ibikoresho bibiri no guhinduranya"},
      ("Availability is part of security (the A in CIA). Redundancy means having spare components, failover is the automatic switch to the spare when something breaks, and a load balancer spreads requests across several servers so no single one is overwhelmed. A single point of failure is any part whose failure stops everything.", "Remove single points of failure for critical services (power, internet link, server, database), monitor health, and test failover on purpose. It also helps absorb DDoS floods. Redundancy is not a backup: a deleted or encrypted file is copied to both sides."),
      ("La disponibilité fait partie de la sécurité (le D de la triade CIA, « A » en anglais). La redondance est d'avoir des composants de rechange, le basculement est le passage automatique vers le secours en cas de panne, et un répartiteur de charge distribue les requêtes entre plusieurs serveurs. Un point de défaillance unique est tout élément dont la panne arrête tout.", "Supprimez les points uniques de défaillance des services critiques (alimentation, lien internet, serveur, base de données), surveillez l'état et testez volontairement le basculement. Cela aide aussi à absorber un DDoS. La redondance n'est pas une sauvegarde : un fichier supprimé ou chiffré est copié des deux côtés."),
      ("Kuboneka ni igice cy'umutekano (A muri CIA). Redundancy ni ukugira ibice by'ingoboka, failover ni ugusimburana kwikora iyo hari ikintu cyangiritse, naho load balancer ikwirakwiza ibyifuzo kuri seriveri nyinshi ngo imwe itarenzwa. Single point of failure ni igice cyose iyo cyangiritse byose bihagarara.", "Kuraho single points of failure kuri serivisi z'ingenzi (amashanyarazi, interineti, seriveri, database), kurikirana imiterere kandi ugerageze failover ku bushake. Bifasha no kwakira DDoS. Redundancy si backup: dosiye yasibwe cyangwa yafunzwe ikopororwa ku mpande zombi."),
      ("Upatikanaji ni sehemu ya usalama (A katika CIA). Uduplishaji ni kuwa na vipengele vya akiba, failover ni kubadilisha kiotomatiki hadi akiba kitu kikiharibika, na load balancer husambaza maombi kwa seva kadhaa ili moja isizidiwe. Single point of failure ni sehemu yoyote ikishindwa kila kitu husimama.", "Ondoa single points of failure kwa huduma muhimu (umeme, kiungo cha intaneti, seva, hifadhidata), fuatilia afya na ujaribu failover kwa makusudi. Pia husaidia kunyonya mafuriko ya DDoS. Uduplishaji si nakala rudufu: faili iliyofutwa au kusimbwa hunakiliwa pande zote.")),
    R("cdn", "Content delivery network (CDN)", ["cdn", "content delivery network", "content distribution network", "cloudflare", "akamai", "edge network"], "network", "map with servers around the world",
      {"fr": "Réseau de diffusion de contenu (CDN)", "sw": "Mtandao wa usambazaji wa maudhui (CDN)", "rw": "Umuyoboro wo gukwirakwiza ibikubiye ku rubuga (CDN)"},
      ("A CDN is a worldwide network of servers that keeps copies of a website's files close to visitors and sits between them and the real (origin) server. It makes sites faster, can absorb DDoS floods, filter bad traffic and hide the origin's address.", "Useful for any site with many visitors. Keep the origin server private (accept traffic only from the CDN), use HTTPS to the origin, and set caching rules carefully so private pages are never cached and served to others."),
      ("Un CDN est un réseau mondial de serveurs qui garde des copies des fichiers d'un site près des visiteurs et se place entre eux et le serveur d'origine. Il accélère les sites, peut absorber des attaques DDoS, filtrer le trafic malveillant et masquer l'adresse de l'origine.", "Utile pour tout site très visité. Gardez le serveur d'origine privé (n'acceptez que le trafic du CDN), utilisez HTTPS vers l'origine et réglez soigneusement le cache pour ne jamais mettre en cache des pages privées."),
      ("CDN ni umuyoboro w'isi yose wa seriveri ubika kopi z'amadosiye y'urubuga hafi y'abarusura, ukaba hagati yabo na seriveri y'ibanze. Utuma imbuga zihuta, ushobora kwakira DDoS, kuyungurura urujya n'uruza rubi no guhisha aderesi y'ibanze.", "Ukwiye ku rubuga urwo ari rwo rwose rufite abasura benshi. Gira seriveri y'ibanze ibanga (yemere urujya n'uruza rwa CDN gusa), koresha HTTPS ujya ku y'ibanze kandi ushyireho amategeko ya cache neza kugira ngo impapuro z'ibanga zitabikwa."),
      ("CDN ni mtandao wa seva duniani kote unaohifadhi nakala za faili za tovuti karibu na wageni na kukaa kati yao na seva asili. Hufanya tovuti ziwe za haraka, unaweza kunyonya mafuriko ya DDoS, kuchuja trafiki mbaya na kuficha anwani ya asili.", "Inafaa kwa tovuti yoyote yenye wageni wengi. Weka seva asili kuwa ya faragha (kubali trafiki ya CDN tu), tumia HTTPS kwenda asili na weka sheria za cache kwa uangalifu ili kurasa za faragha zisihifadhiwe.")),
    R("osint-recon-tools", "OSINT tools (Maltego, theHarvester, Recon-ng)", ["maltego", "theharvester", "the harvester", "recon-ng", "recon ng", "osint tools", "osint framework", "link analysis tool", "spiderfoot"], "operations", "web of connected names and domains",
      {"fr": "Outils OSINT", "sw": "Zana za OSINT", "rw": "Ibikoresho bya OSINT"},
      ("Tools that collect and connect public information: Maltego draws link graphs between people, companies, domains and emails; theHarvester gathers email addresses, subdomains and names from public sources; Recon-ng and SpiderFoot automate public-source reconnaissance. Attackers use the same data to plan phishing.", "Defenders use them on their own organisation to see what an attacker could learn (exposed emails, forgotten subdomains, leaked staff details) and reduce it. Use them only within the law and on targets you are authorised to assess."),
      ("Outils qui collectent et relient des informations publiques : Maltego dessine des graphes de liens entre personnes, entreprises, domaines et e-mails ; theHarvester récupère adresses e-mail, sous-domaines et noms depuis des sources publiques ; Recon-ng et SpiderFoot automatisent la reconnaissance en sources ouvertes. Les attaquants utilisent les mêmes données pour préparer du phishing.", "Les défenseurs les utilisent sur leur propre organisation pour voir ce qu'un attaquant pourrait apprendre (e-mails exposés, sous-domaines oubliés, détails du personnel) et le réduire. Utilisez-les dans la loi et sur des cibles autorisées."),
      ("Ibikoresho bikusanya bikanahuza amakuru ya rubanda: Maltego ishushanya isano hagati y'abantu, ibigo, domains na imeri; theHarvester ikusanya imeri, subdomains n'amazina ahari ku mugaragaro; Recon-ng na SpiderFoot byikoresha gutohoza amakuru ya rubanda. Abagizi ba nabi bakoresha ayo makuru bategura phishing.", "Abarinzi babikoresha ku kigo cyabo ngo barebe icyo umushimusi yamenya (imeri zigaragara, subdomains zibagiranye, amakuru y'abakozi yamenetse) bakagabanya. Bikoreshwe mu mategeko no ku ntego wemerewe gusuzuma."),
      ("Zana zinazokusanya na kuunganisha taarifa za umma: Maltego huchora michoro ya viungo kati ya watu, kampuni, vikoa na barua pepe; theHarvester hukusanya barua pepe, subdomains na majina kutoka vyanzo vya umma; Recon-ng na SpiderFoot hujiendesha upelelezi wa vyanzo wazi. Washambulizi hutumia data hiyo kupanga hadaa.", "Watetezi huzitumia kwa shirika lao kuona mshambulizi angejifunza nini (barua pepe zilizofichuliwa, subdomains zilizosahaulika, taarifa za wafanyakazi) na kupunguza. Zitumie ndani ya sheria na kwa walengwa uliowaruhusiwa kutathmini.")),
    R("ad-testing-tools", "BloodHound, Impacket and Responder (Active Directory testing tools)", ["bloodhound", "impacket", "responder tool", "responder", "crackmapexec", "netexec", "ad attack path", "active directory testing tools", "llmnr poisoning tool"], "operations", "graph of network paths to an admin account",
      {"fr": "BloodHound, Impacket et Responder", "sw": "BloodHound, Impacket na Responder", "rw": "BloodHound, Impacket na Responder"},
      ("Well-known tools for testing Windows/Active Directory networks: BloodHound maps the chains of permissions that lead to administrator accounts, Impacket is a library for working with network protocols, and Responder answers name-lookup broadcasts (LLMNR/NBT-NS) to capture login hashes. Criminals and authorised testers both use them.", "Defenders run BloodHound on their own domain to cut dangerous permission paths, and switch off LLMNR/NBT-NS, require SMB signing, use strong unique admin passwords and limit who has domain admin rights. Run such tools only with written permission."),
      ("Outils connus pour tester les réseaux Windows/Active Directory : BloodHound cartographie les chaînes de droits menant aux comptes administrateurs, Impacket est une bibliothèque pour manipuler des protocoles réseau et Responder répond aux diffusions de résolution de noms (LLMNR/NBT-NS) pour capturer des empreintes de connexion. Criminels et testeurs autorisés les utilisent.", "Les défenseurs lancent BloodHound sur leur propre domaine pour couper les chemins de droits dangereux, désactivent LLMNR/NBT-NS, exigent la signature SMB, utilisent des mots de passe admin forts et uniques et limitent les droits d'administrateur de domaine. N'exécutez ces outils qu'avec autorisation écrite."),
      ("Ibikoresho bizwi byo gusuzuma imiyoboro ya Windows/Active Directory: BloodHound ishushanya imikoranire y'uburenganzira igeza kuri konti z'abayobozi, Impacket ni isomero ryo gukorana na protocols z'umuyoboro, na Responder isubiza ibibazo byo gushaka amazina (LLMNR/NBT-NS) ikavomera hash z'ubwinjira. Abagizi ba nabi n'abasuzuma bemerewe barabikoresha.", "Abarinzi bakoresha BloodHound ku muyoboro wabo bagaca inzira z'uburenganzira zishobora guteza ibyago, bagahagarika LLMNR/NBT-NS, bagasaba SMB signing, bagakoresha amagambo y'ibanga akomeye kandi yihariye ku bayobozi kandi bakagabanya abafite uburenganzira bwo hejuru. Bikoreshwe gusa ufite uruhushya rwanditse."),
      ("Zana zinazojulikana za kupima mitandao ya Windows/Active Directory: BloodHound huchora minyororo ya ruhusa inayoongoza kwenye akaunti za wasimamizi, Impacket ni maktaba ya kufanya kazi na itifaki za mtandao, na Responder hujibu matangazo ya kutafuta majina (LLMNR/NBT-NS) kunasa hashi za kuingia. Wahalifu na wapimaji walioruhusiwa wote huzitumia.", "Watetezi huendesha BloodHound kwenye kikoa chao kukata njia hatari za ruhusa, huzima LLMNR/NBT-NS, kudai SMB signing, kutumia nywila imara za kipekee kwa wasimamizi na kupunguza wenye haki za juu. Tumia zana hizi kwa idhini ya maandishi tu.")),
    R("sysinternals-osquery", "Sysinternals and osquery (endpoint visibility tools)", ["sysinternals", "sysmon", "process explorer", "autoruns", "process monitor", "procmon", "osquery", "endpoint visibility", "endpoint telemetry"], "operations", "dashboard of running programs on a laptop",
      {"fr": "Sysinternals et osquery", "sw": "Sysinternals na osquery", "rw": "Sysinternals na osquery"},
      ("Free tools that show what a computer is really doing. Microsoft Sysinternals includes Process Explorer (running programs), Autoruns (what starts at boot), Process Monitor (file and registry activity) and Sysmon (detailed security logging). osquery lets you ask questions about devices with SQL-like queries.", "Defenders and incident responders use them to spot odd programs, persistence and suspicious connections, and to feed logs to a SIEM. Download them only from the official vendor page, because fake copies of admin tools carry malware."),
      ("Outils gratuits qui montrent ce que fait vraiment un ordinateur. Microsoft Sysinternals comprend Process Explorer (programmes actifs), Autoruns (ce qui démarre au boot), Process Monitor (activité fichiers et registre) et Sysmon (journalisation de sécurité détaillée). osquery interroge les appareils avec des requêtes de type SQL.", "Défenseurs et équipes de réponse s'en servent pour repérer programmes étranges, persistance et connexions suspectes, et alimenter un SIEM. Téléchargez-les uniquement sur la page officielle de l'éditeur : de fausses copies d'outils d'administration contiennent des malwares."),
      ("Ibikoresho by'ubuntu byerekana ibyo mudasobwa ikora koko. Microsoft Sysinternals irimo Process Explorer (porogaramu ziri gukora), Autoruns (ibitangira ku gutangira), Process Monitor (ibikorwa kuri dosiye na registry) na Sysmon (logs z'umutekano zirambuye). osquery igufasha kubaza ibikoresho ukoresheje ibibazo bimeze nka SQL.", "Abarinzi n'abasubiza ibitero babikoresha kubona porogaramu zidasanzwe, persistence n'ihuzwa rikekwa, no kugaburira SIEM. Bikure ku rubuga rwemewe rw'uwabikoze gusa kuko kopi z'impimbano z'ibikoresho by'ubuyobozi zirimo malware."),
      ("Zana za bure zinazoonyesha kompyuta inafanya nini kweli. Microsoft Sysinternals ina Process Explorer (programu zinazoendeshwa), Autoruns (kinachoanza wakati wa kuwasha), Process Monitor (shughuli za faili na rejista) na Sysmon (kumbukumbu za usalama za kina). osquery hukuwezesha kuuliza vifaa kwa maswali kama SQL.", "Watetezi na wajibu matukio huzitumia kuona programu za ajabu, persistence na miunganisho ya kutiliwa shaka, na kulisha SIEM. Zipakue kutoka ukurasa rasmi wa muuzaji tu, kwa sababu nakala bandia za zana za usimamizi zina programu hasidi.")),
    R("linux-hardening-tools", "Linux firewalls and hardening (iptables, nftables, ufw, SELinux, AppArmor, chroot)", ["iptables", "nftables", "ufw", "uncomplicated firewall", "selinux", "apparmor", "chroot", "linux firewall", "linux hardening", "mandatory access control", "fail2ban", "linux security"], "defense", "penguin behind a wall",
      {"fr": "Pare-feu et durcissement Linux", "sw": "Firewall na uimarishaji wa Linux", "rw": "Firewall n'gushimangira umutekano wa Linux"},
      ("Built-in Linux protections: iptables and its successor nftables filter packets, ufw is a simple front-end, fail2ban blocks addresses that keep failing to log in, SELinux and AppArmor confine each program to what it needs (mandatory access control), and chroot limits a program's view of the file system (useful, but not a strong boundary alone).", "A basic hardening routine: enable the firewall with default deny, open only needed ports, use SSH keys and disable root and password login, install updates, remove unused services, keep SELinux/AppArmor on, and review logs."),
      ("Protections intégrées de Linux : iptables et son successeur nftables filtrent les paquets, ufw en est une interface simple, fail2ban bloque les adresses qui échouent sans cesse à se connecter, SELinux et AppArmor confinent chaque programme à ce dont il a besoin (contrôle d'accès obligatoire) et chroot limite la vue d'un programme sur les fichiers (utile, mais pas une barrière solide seule).", "Routine de durcissement de base : activer le pare-feu en refus par défaut, n'ouvrir que les ports nécessaires, utiliser des clés SSH et désactiver la connexion root et par mot de passe, installer les mises à jour, retirer les services inutiles, garder SELinux/AppArmor actifs et lire les journaux."),
      ("Uburyo Linux ifite bwo kurinda: iptables n'uyisimbuye nftables bayungurura ibipaki by'umuyoboro, ufw ni ubworoherezi bwabyo, fail2ban ihagarika aderesi zikomeza kunanirwa kwinjira, SELinux na AppArmor ni mandatory access control (buri porogaramu igarukira ku byo ikeneye) naho chroot ikumira icyo porogaramu ibona muri sisitemu ya dosiye (ifasha ariko si urukuta rukomeye ubwayo).", "Gahunda y'ibanze yo gushimangira: fungura firewall yanga byose mbere, fungura ports zikenewe gusa, koresha SSH keys uhagarike root na password login, shyiraho ivugurura, kuraho serivisi zitari ngombwa, usige SELinux/AppArmor bikora kandi usome logs."),
      ("Kinga zilizojengwa ndani ya Linux: iptables na mrithi wake nftables huchuja pakiti za mtandao, ufw ni kiolesura rahisi chake, fail2ban huzuia anwani zinazoshindwa kuingia mara kwa mara, SELinux na AppArmor ni udhibiti wa lazima wa ufikiaji (kila programu inazuiwa kwa inachohitaji) na chroot hupunguza mtazamo wa programu kwenye mfumo wa faili (inasaidia, lakini si ukuta imara peke yake).", "Utaratibu wa msingi wa kuimarisha: washa firewall ikikataa kila kitu kwanza, fungua port zinazohitajika tu, tumia funguo za SSH na uzime kuingia kwa root na nywila, sakinisha masasisho, ondoa huduma zisizotumika, acha SELinux/AppArmor zikiwa zimewashwa na usome kumbukumbu.")),
    R("firewall-products", "Firewall and security vendors (pfSense, OPNsense, Fortinet, Palo Alto, Cisco)", ["pfsense", "opnsense", "fortinet", "fortigate", "palo alto", "palo alto networks", "cisco asa", "cisco firepower", "sophos", "check point", "firewall products", "firewall vendors", "firewall brands"], "network", "rack-mounted firewall appliance",
      {"fr": "Pare-feu : produits et éditeurs", "sw": "Bidhaa za firewall", "rw": "Ibikoresho bya firewall n'ababikora"},
      ("Firewalls come as open-source software (pfSense, OPNsense), commercial next-generation appliances (Fortinet FortiGate, Palo Alto Networks, Check Point, Sophos) and older enterprise lines (Cisco ASA and Firepower). All filter traffic by rules, and most add VPN, intrusion prevention and web filtering.", "Choose by need, budget and skills, not brand. Whatever you use, keep its firmware patched (internet-facing firewalls and VPN gateways are frequent targets), change default passwords, restrict the admin interface and back up the configuration."),
      ("Les pare-feu existent en logiciel libre (pfSense, OPNsense), en équipements commerciaux de nouvelle génération (Fortinet FortiGate, Palo Alto Networks, Check Point, Sophos) et en gammes d'entreprise plus anciennes (Cisco ASA et Firepower). Tous filtrent le trafic selon des règles et la plupart ajoutent VPN, prévention d'intrusion et filtrage web.", "Choisissez selon besoin, budget et compétences, pas selon la marque. Quel que soit le produit, gardez son micrologiciel à jour (pare-feu et passerelles VPN exposés sont des cibles fréquentes), changez les mots de passe par défaut, restreignez l'interface d'administration et sauvegardez la configuration."),
      ("Firewall ziri mu bwoko: porogaramu y'ubuntu (pfSense, OPNsense), ibikoresho by'ubucuruzi bigezweho (Fortinet FortiGate, Palo Alto Networks, Check Point, Sophos) n'ibya kera by'ibigo (Cisco ASA na Firepower). Zose ziyungurura urujya n'uruza zikurikije amategeko, kandi nyinshi zongeraho VPN, intrusion prevention no kuyungurura urubuga.", "Hitamo hakurikijwe ibikenewe, ingengo y'imari n'ubumenyi, si ikirango. Icyo ukoresha cyose, gihore gifite firmware ivuguruye (firewalls na VPN gateways biri kuri interineti ni intego zikunze), hindura ijambo ry'ibanga ryashyizweho, ugabanye aho bayoborerwa kandi ubike configuration."),
      ("Firewall zipo kama programu huria (pfSense, OPNsense), vifaa vya kibiashara vya kizazi kipya (Fortinet FortiGate, Palo Alto Networks, Check Point, Sophos) na mistari ya zamani ya makampuni (Cisco ASA na Firepower). Zote huchuja trafiki kwa sheria na nyingi huongeza VPN, kuzuia uvamizi na kuchuja wavuti.", "Chagua kulingana na mahitaji, bajeti na ujuzi, si chapa. Chochote unachotumia, weka firmware iliyosasishwa (firewall na lango za VPN zilizo mtandaoni ni walengwa wa mara kwa mara), badilisha nywila chaguo-msingi, punguza kiolesura cha usimamizi na hifadhi nakala ya usanidi.")),
    R("mtls-api-gateway", "Mutual TLS (mTLS), API gateways and service mesh", ["mtls", "mutual tls", "two-way tls", "client certificate authentication", "api gateway", "service mesh", "istio", "linkerd", "zero trust between services"], "appsec", "two keys opening one door at once",
      {"fr": "TLS mutuel (mTLS), passerelles d'API et maillage de services", "sw": "mTLS, lango la API na service mesh", "rw": "mTLS, API gateway na service mesh"},
      ("In ordinary TLS only the server proves who it is; in mutual TLS (mTLS) both sides present certificates, so each knows exactly who it is talking to. An API gateway is a single front door for APIs that enforces login, rate limits and logging, and a service mesh adds automatic mTLS and policy between many small services.", "Use mTLS between internal services and for sensitive partner connections, and put authentication, throttling and monitoring in the gateway rather than in every service. Certificates must be issued, rotated and revoked properly, or mTLS becomes a source of outages."),
      ("Dans un TLS ordinaire seul le serveur prouve son identité ; en TLS mutuel (mTLS) les deux parties présentent un certificat, chacune sait donc précisément avec qui elle parle. Une passerelle d'API est une porte d'entrée unique pour les API qui impose authentification, limites de débit et journalisation, et un maillage de services ajoute mTLS et politiques automatiques entre de nombreux petits services.", "Utilisez le mTLS entre services internes et pour les connexions sensibles avec des partenaires ; placez authentification, limitation et supervision dans la passerelle plutôt que dans chaque service. Les certificats doivent être émis, renouvelés et révoqués correctement, sinon le mTLS cause des pannes."),
      ("Muri TLS isanzwe seriveri yonyine yerekana uwo ari we; muri mutual TLS (mTLS) impande zombi zerekana certificates, bityo buri ruhande rumenya neza uwo rubwira. API gateway ni umuryango umwe w'imbere wa API uhatira kwinjira, imbibi z'ibyifuzo na logs, naho service mesh yongeraho mTLS n'amategeko byikora hagati ya serivisi nyinshi nto.", "Koresha mTLS hagati ya serivisi z'imbere no ku mpuzamahuza z'abafatanyabikorwa z'ingenzi, kandi shyira kwemeza, imbibi no gukurikirana muri gateway aho kuba muri buri serivisi. Certificates zigomba gutangwa, guhindurwa no gukurwaho neza, bitaba ibyo mTLS itera guhagarara."),
      ("Katika TLS ya kawaida seva pekee ndiyo inayothibitisha utambulisho; katika mutual TLS (mTLS) pande zote huwasilisha vyeti, hivyo kila mmoja anajua anaongea na nani. API gateway ni mlango mmoja wa mbele wa API unaotekeleza kuingia, mipaka ya maombi na kumbukumbu, na service mesh huongeza mTLS na sera kiotomatiki kati ya huduma ndogo nyingi.", "Tumia mTLS kati ya huduma za ndani na kwa miunganisho nyeti ya washirika, na weka uthibitishaji, udhibiti wa kasi na ufuatiliaji kwenye gateway badala ya kila huduma. Vyeti lazima vitolewe, vibadilishwe na kufutwa ipasavyo, vinginevyo mTLS husababisha kukatika kwa huduma.")),
    R("ssh-tunneling", "SSH tunnelling and port forwarding", ["ssh tunnel", "ssh tunneling", "ssh tunnelling", "port forwarding", "ssh port forwarding", "reverse ssh tunnel", "dynamic port forwarding", "socks over ssh"], "network", "tunnel carrying traffic through a mountain",
      {"fr": "Tunnels SSH et redirection de ports", "sw": "Tunnel za SSH na kupeleka port", "rw": "Tunnel za SSH no kohereza port"},
      ("SSH can carry other network traffic inside its encrypted connection (a tunnel). Administrators use it to reach internal services safely; attackers use the same feature to slip traffic past firewalls or keep a hidden way back in (a reverse tunnel).", "Allow SSH only from trusted addresses with keys and MFA, disable forwarding where it is not needed, monitor for long-lived or unusual SSH connections, and block outbound SSH from servers that have no reason to make it."),
      ("SSH peut transporter d'autres flux réseau dans sa connexion chiffrée (un tunnel). Les administrateurs l'utilisent pour atteindre des services internes en sécurité ; les attaquants emploient la même fonction pour faire passer du trafic à travers les pare-feu ou garder une porte dérobée (tunnel inversé).", "N'autorisez SSH que depuis des adresses de confiance avec clés et MFA, désactivez la redirection quand elle est inutile, surveillez les connexions SSH longues ou inhabituelles et bloquez le SSH sortant des serveurs qui n'en ont pas besoin."),
      ("SSH ishobora gutwara urundi rujya n'uruza rw'umuyoboro mu isano yayo ifunzwe (tunnel). Abayobozi barayikoresha bagera kuri serivisi z'imbere mu buryo butekanye; abagizi ba nabi bakoresha iyo mikorere kunyuza amakuru hejuru ya firewall cyangwa gukomeza inzira ihishe (reverse tunnel).", "Emera SSH gusa ivuye ku ma aderesi yizewe ifite keys na MFA, hagarika forwarding aho itari ngombwa, kurikirana isano za SSH zimara igihe kirekire cyangwa zidasanzwe kandi uhagarike SSH isohoka kuri seriveri zitayikeneye."),
      ("SSH inaweza kubeba trafiki nyingine ya mtandao ndani ya muunganisho wake uliosimbwa (tunnel). Wasimamizi huitumia kufikia huduma za ndani kwa usalama; washambulizi hutumia kipengele hicho hicho kupitisha trafiki kupitia firewall au kuweka njia ya siri ya kurudi (reverse tunnel).", "Ruhusu SSH kutoka anwani zinazoaminika tu kwa funguo na MFA, zima forwarding pale isipohitajika, fuatilia miunganisho ya SSH ya muda mrefu au isiyo ya kawaida na uzuie SSH inayotoka kwa seva zisizo na sababu ya kuitumia.")),
    R("tails-whonix", "Tails and Whonix (privacy-focused operating systems)", ["tails", "tails os", "whonix", "amnesic live system", "privacy operating system", "tor operating system", "qubes os", "qubes"], "privacy", "usb stick with a mask",
      {"fr": "Tails et Whonix", "sw": "Tails na Whonix", "rw": "Tails na Whonix"},
      ("Tails is an operating system that runs from a USB stick, sends all internet traffic through Tor and leaves no trace on the computer when shut down. Whonix runs in two virtual machines so that all traffic is forced through Tor. Qubes OS isolates activities in separate compartments.", "They help journalists, activists and people at risk to protect their privacy and sources. They are not magic: Tor does not hide what you type into a site you log into, and mistakes (using real names, downloading and opening files) can still identify you."),
      ("Tails est un système qui démarre depuis une clé USB, fait passer tout le trafic internet par Tor et ne laisse aucune trace sur l'ordinateur à l'arrêt. Whonix tourne dans deux machines virtuelles qui forcent le trafic à passer par Tor. Qubes OS isole les activités dans des compartiments séparés.", "Ils aident journalistes, militants et personnes menacées à protéger leur vie privée et leurs sources. Ce n'est pas magique : Tor ne cache pas ce que vous saisissez sur un site où vous vous connectez, et des erreurs (noms réels, ouverture de fichiers téléchargés) peuvent vous identifier."),
      ("Tails ni sisitemu ikora ivuye kuri USB, inyuza amakuru yose ya interineti kuri Tor kandi ntisiga ikimenyetso kuri mudasobwa iyo izimijwe. Whonix ikora mu mashini ebyiri za virtual zihatira amakuru gunyura kuri Tor. Qubes OS itandukanya ibikorwa mu bice bitandukanye.", "Bifasha abanyamakuru, abaharanira ibyiza n'abari mu kaga kurinda ibanga ryabo n'inkomoko zabo. Si igitangaza: Tor ntihisha ibyo wandika ku rubuga winjiramo, kandi amakosa (gukoresha amazina nyayo, gufungura dosiye wakuyeho) ashobora kukumenyekanisha."),
      ("Tails ni mfumo unaoendeshwa kutoka USB, hupitisha trafiki yote ya intaneti kupitia Tor na haachi alama kwenye kompyuta ikizimwa. Whonix huendeshwa kwenye mashine mbili pepe zinazolazimisha trafiki kupitia Tor. Qubes OS hutenga shughuli katika sehemu tofauti.", "Husaidia waandishi wa habari, wanaharakati na walio hatarini kulinda faragha na vyanzo vyao. Si uchawi: Tor haifichi unachoandika kwenye tovuti unayoingia, na makosa (kutumia majina halisi, kufungua faili ulizopakua) yanaweza kukutambulisha.")),
    R("ech-hsts-preload", "Encrypted Client Hello (ECH) and HSTS preload", ["ech", "encrypted client hello", "esni", "encrypted sni", "server name indication", "sni", "hsts preload", "hsts preload list", "preload list"], "network", "envelope hiding the address line",
      {"fr": "Encrypted Client Hello (ECH) et préchargement HSTS", "sw": "ECH na HSTS preload", "rw": "ECH na HSTS preload"},
      ("When your browser opens an HTTPS connection it normally reveals the site name (SNI) in clear text; Encrypted Client Hello (ECH, successor of ESNI) encrypts that name so observers see less. HSTS preload is a list built into browsers that forces HTTPS for a site from the very first visit, preventing SSL-stripping downgrades.", "Site owners should enable HTTPS everywhere, HSTS (and preload when ready) and, where supported, ECH. Users benefit automatically from up-to-date browsers; ECH hides names from observers but not from the site itself or the DNS if that is not encrypted."),
      ("Quand un navigateur ouvre une connexion HTTPS il révèle normalement le nom du site (SNI) en clair ; Encrypted Client Hello (ECH, successeur d'ESNI) chiffre ce nom pour que les observateurs voient moins. Le préchargement HSTS est une liste intégrée aux navigateurs qui impose HTTPS dès la première visite, empêchant les attaques de rétrogradation (SSL stripping).", "Les propriétaires de sites doivent activer HTTPS partout, HSTS (et le préchargement quand prêt) et, si possible, ECH. Les utilisateurs en profitent avec un navigateur à jour ; ECH cache le nom aux observateurs mais pas au site lui-même ni au DNS s'il n'est pas chiffré."),
      ("Iyo mushakisha ifunguye isano ya HTTPS isanzwe yerekana izina ry'urubuga (SNI) ridafunze; Encrypted Client Hello (ECH, usimbura ESNI) rifunga iryo zina ngo ababireba babone bike. HSTS preload ni urutonde ruri muri mushakisha ruhatira HTTPS kuva ku musura wa mbere, rukabuza ibitero byo kumanura (SSL stripping).", "Banyiri imbuga bagomba gukoresha HTTPS hose, HSTS (na preload iyo biteguye) na ECH aho ishoboka. Abakoresha babyungukiramo bafite mushakisha ivuguruye; ECH ihisha izina ababireba ariko ntiriryihishe urubuga ubwarwo cyangwa DNS idafunze."),
      ("Kivinjari kinapofungua muunganisho wa HTTPS kwa kawaida hufichua jina la tovuti (SNI) wazi; Encrypted Client Hello (ECH, mrithi wa ESNI) husimba jina hilo ili watazamaji waone kidogo. HSTS preload ni orodha iliyojengwa kwenye vivinjari inayolazimisha HTTPS tangu ziara ya kwanza, kuzuia mashambulizi ya kushusha (SSL stripping).", "Wamiliki wa tovuti wanapaswa kuwasha HTTPS kila mahali, HSTS (na preload ikiwa tayari) na ECH inapoungwa mkono. Watumiaji hufaidika kwa kivinjari kilichosasishwa; ECH huficha jina kwa watazamaji lakini si kwa tovuti yenyewe wala DNS isiyosimbwa.")),
    R("secure-messaging-apps", "Secure messaging apps and disappearing messages", ["secure messaging", "secure messenger", "signal app", "signal messenger", "whatsapp encryption", "disappearing messages", "safety numbers", "encrypted chat", "encrypted messaging apps", "e2ee messaging", "telegram secret chats"], "privacy", "chat bubble with a padlock",
      {"fr": "Messageries sécurisées et messages éphémères", "sw": "Programu salama za ujumbe na ujumbe unaopotea", "rw": "Porogaramu z'ubutumwa zirinzwe n'ubutumwa bwisiba"},
      ("Secure messengers use end-to-end encryption so only you and the person you write to can read the messages (Signal and WhatsApp do this by default; Telegram only in optional ‘secret chats’). Disappearing messages delete chats after a set time, and safety numbers let you verify you are talking to the right person.", "Choose an app your contacts use, verify safety numbers for sensitive talks, lock the app, and remember limits: metadata (who talks to whom, when) may still be visible, screenshots and cloud backups can leak chats, and a stolen unlocked phone exposes everything."),
      ("Les messageries sécurisées utilisent le chiffrement de bout en bout : seuls vous et votre correspondant lisez les messages (Signal et WhatsApp le font par défaut ; Telegram seulement dans des « discussions secrètes » optionnelles). Les messages éphémères effacent les discussions après un délai et les numéros de sécurité permettent de vérifier votre interlocuteur.", "Choisissez une application utilisée par vos contacts, vérifiez les numéros de sécurité pour les échanges sensibles, verrouillez l'application et gardez les limites en tête : les métadonnées (qui parle à qui, quand) peuvent rester visibles, captures d'écran et sauvegardes cloud peuvent faire fuiter les discussions, et un téléphone volé déverrouillé expose tout."),
      ("Porogaramu z'ubutumwa zirinzwe zikoresha end-to-end encryption: wowe n'uwo wandikira gusa ni mwe musoma ubutumwa (Signal na WhatsApp bibikora ku buryo busanzwe; Telegram gusa mu «secret chats» zihitamo). Ubutumwa bwisiba busiba ibiganiro nyuma y'igihe kigenwe, naho safety numbers zigufasha kwemeza ko ubwira umuntu nyawe.", "Hitamo porogaramu abo muvugana bakoresha, emeza safety numbers ku biganiro by'ingenzi, ufunge porogaramu kandi wibuke imbibi: metadata (ukivugana n'uwo, ryari) ishobora kugaragara, screenshots na backups za cloud bishobora kumena ibiganiro, na telefone yibwe idafunze igaragaza byose."),
      ("Programu salama za ujumbe hutumia usimbaji wa mwanzo hadi mwisho (E2EE) ili wewe na unayemwandikia tu mnaweza kusoma (Signal na WhatsApp hufanya hivyo kwa chaguo-msingi; Telegram tu kwenye ‘secret chats’ za hiari). Ujumbe unaopotea hufuta mazungumzo baada ya muda uliowekwa, na namba za usalama hukuwezesha kuthibitisha unaongea na mtu sahihi.", "Chagua programu wanayotumia wawasiliani wako, thibitisha namba za usalama kwa mazungumzo nyeti, funga programu na ukumbuke mipaka: metadata (nani anaongea na nani, lini) inaweza kuonekana, picha za skrini na nakala za cloud zinaweza kuvujisha mazungumzo, na simu iliyoibiwa isiyofungwa hufichua kila kitu.")),
    R("web-tracking", "Tracking cookies, web beacons, supercookies and session replay", ["tracking cookie", "tracking cookies", "third party cookie", "third-party cookies", "web beacon", "tracking pixel", "supercookie", "evercookie", "zombie cookie", "session replay", "cross-site tracking", "online tracking", "ad tracking", "do not track"], "privacy", "footprints following a browser",
      {"fr": "Cookies de pistage, pixels espions, supercookies et relecture de session", "sw": "Cookies za ufuatiliaji, web beacons na session replay", "rw": "Cookies zikurikirana, web beacons na session replay"},
      ("Websites and advertisers follow you across the web with third-party tracking cookies, tiny invisible images called web beacons or tracking pixels, hard-to-delete supercookies, and session-replay scripts that record clicks and typing. Together with fingerprinting they build a profile of your habits.", "Reduce it: block third-party cookies, use a browser with tracking protection or a content blocker, decline non-essential cookies, clear site data, limit app permissions and ad-ID tracking on your phone, and never type secrets into sites you do not trust."),
      ("Sites et annonceurs vous suivent sur le web avec des cookies tiers de pistage, de minuscules images invisibles appelées pixels espions (web beacons), des supercookies difficiles à supprimer et des scripts de relecture de session qui enregistrent clics et frappes. Avec l'empreinte du navigateur, ils construisent un profil de vos habitudes.", "Réduisez-le : bloquez les cookies tiers, utilisez un navigateur avec protection contre le pistage ou un bloqueur de contenu, refusez les cookies non essentiels, effacez les données de site, limitez permissions des applis et identifiant publicitaire sur le téléphone, et ne saisissez jamais de secrets sur un site douteux."),
      ("Imbuga n'abamamaza bagukurikira kuri murandasi bakoresha cookies z'abandi zikurikirana, amashusho mato atagaragara yitwa web beacons cyangwa tracking pixels, supercookies zigoye gusiba, na session replay zandika gukanda no kwandika. Hamwe na fingerprinting bubaka umwirondoro w'imigirire yawe.", "Kugabanya: hagarika cookies z'abandi, koresha mushakisha irinda gukurikirwa cyangwa content blocker, anga cookies zitari ngombwa, siba amakuru y'urubuga, ugabanye uburenganzira bwa porogaramu n'ad-ID kuri telefone, kandi ntuzigere wandika ibanga ku rubuga utizeye."),
      ("Tovuti na watangazaji hukufuata mtandaoni kwa cookies za wahusika wengine za ufuatiliaji, picha ndogo zisizoonekana zinazoitwa web beacons au tracking pixels, supercookies ngumu kufuta, na skripti za session replay zinazorekodi mibofyo na uandishi. Pamoja na fingerprinting hujenga wasifu wa tabia zako.", "Punguza: zuia cookies za wahusika wengine, tumia kivinjari chenye ulinzi wa ufuatiliaji au kizuizi cha maudhui, kataa cookies zisizo za lazima, futa data ya tovuti, punguza ruhusa za programu na kitambulisho cha matangazo kwenye simu, na usiandike siri kwenye tovuti usiyoiamini.")),
]
